  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 156 PM MDT Sun Aug 9 2026\n\nShort term impacts will again be some air quality issues with\nsmoke persisting throughout all of southeast Idaho to some\nextent. Will remain very hot through Tuesday with low elevation\nhighs remaining in the 90s but think triple digit highs are done\nfor now. Will have some convective activity but very isolated\nthis afternoon and evening and Monday mainly in the southern\nmountains. Afternoons both today and Monday will be breezy with\nwidespread 20 to 30 mph gusts especially on Monday afternoon.\nOther issue will be a pattern change expected Wednesday through\nnext weekend with wetter and cooler conditions expected. Have\nmuch higher chance of showers and thunderstorms Thursday through\nSunday. High temperatures are expected to be well below normal\nas well mid week through next weekend for a change as well.\nMainly 70s and 80s with some days in the 60s mountains.",
